# Marketplace settings

The marketplace is **desktop-owned code**: UI is the fork package `ui-settings-market` (settings section `market`, registers only when `window.shell` exposes the market API), engine is main-process `marketplace-catalog.js` / `marketplace-install.js` over `shell:*` IPC — the curated catalog is the single install path. `dshmarket` is `DROPPED` (not mounted, hidden from the catalog, install rejected; files stay on disk). Dropped matching is family-wide: `isDroppedPluginName` also matches the exact unscoped basename (`DROPPED_BASENAMES`), so scope/owner renames like `@changfenhuang/dsh-genui` stay dropped across catalog, installs, and profile stripping. `fetchRegistry` caps the registry body at 8 MiB (stream-enforced); the Discover tab renders 60 cards per page with a show-more button. Startup runs `removeDshMarketPreset` cleanup only (managed patch block, `desktop-plugins/dshmarket` copy, preset symlink) — never restore `ensureDshMarketPlugin`, extraResources packaging of dshmarket, or a standalone market BrowserWindow. `vendor/dshmarket` is an attribution stub only (LICENSE + `DESKTOP-FORK.md`; source snapshot deleted). Upstream theme shop / backup / diagnostics / hot-update / multi-registry / trial are a v1 product cut — won't port. Installs land in `dsh-home/profiles/web`; restart stays with HarnessController. In-chat `install_dsh_plugin` rides the loopback install-control endpoint only (`github:owner/repo[#ref]`, main-process re-validation + dropped-family rejection); `#path:` specs stay curated-catalog-only. Every install/update channel (catalog id, in-chat, launcher import, update) validates the added package has a loadable entry and a manifest with non-empty `name` + `version` — a versionless manifest breaks the request-time plugin inventory, so failure removes the package and rolls back new dependencies; `desktop-install`'s overlay dir ships its own `package.json` for the same reason.

